  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer gives full scale deflection with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>006</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;current. By connecting it to a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4990</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math> resistance, it can be converted into a voltmeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi></math>. If connected to a <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>249</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance, it becomes an ammeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given a galvanometer of resistance (of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></math>) get converted into a voltmeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>V</mi></math> , when a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4990</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> is connected in series of it and give full scale of deflection with current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>006</mn><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0024_0d45d3468184.png\"/><br/>Than from equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.006</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mrow><mn>4990</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math></p><p>Now this galvanometer is connected with a shunt resistance to convert into ammeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi></math><br/><img src=\"assets\\st0024_ec6debd23a72.png\"/><br >Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.006</mn></math>, so current passing shunt will be <br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>006</mn><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1.494</mn><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi></math><br >Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></msub></math> are in parallel, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></msub></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.006</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.494</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mn>249</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math> ;   <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo></math>given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mn>249</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>  <br ><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
